00000,\"duration\":84800000}],\"raw\":[{\"text\":\"Coral reefs are among the most diverse ecosystems in the ocean. Although they cover only a small portion of the sea floor, they provide shelter and food for thousands of marine species. Corals may look like colorful rocks, but they are actually living organisms. Tiny animals called coral polyps build hard structures that eventually form reefs. Coral reefs are important to people as well.\",\"offset\":10400000,\"duration\":309200000},{\"text\":\"They can help protect coastlines from strong waves and provide income for communities through fishing and tourism. However, reefs face serious threats. Rising ocean temperatures, pollution, destructive fishing practices, and other environmental changes can damage coral ecosystems. Protecting coral reefs requires cooperation among governments, communities, scientists, and individuals.\",\"offset\":322200000,\"duration\":322100000},{\"text\":\"Reducing pollution and using marine resources responsibly can help preserve these ecosystems for future generations.\",\"offset\":647600000,\"duration\":84800000}],\"diagnostics\":{\"recognizedResults\":3,\"wordEvidence\":127,\"recognizingResults\":120,\"noMatchResults\":0,\"canceledResults\":1,\"audioBytesReceived\":2456320,\"sessionStarted\":true,\"sessionStopped\":true,\"serviceConnected\":true,\"lastRecognizedText\":\"Reducing pollution and using marine resources responsibly can help preserve these ecosystems for future generations.\",\"sdkVersion\":\"1.34.0\",\"jsonWordEvidence\":127,\"sdkWordEvidence\":127,\"resultJsonBytes\":34465,\"audioWriterAlive\":false,\"writerFailed\":false},\"error\":null,\"finalSeen\":true,\"doneSeen\":true},\"realtime\":{\"transcript\":\"Coral reefs are among the most diverse ecosystems in the ocean. Although they cover only a small portion of the sea floor, they provide shelter and food for thousands of marine species. Corals may look like colorful rocks, but they are actually living organisms. Tiny anima