e plants needed more water. Instead of using only the school\'s water supply, the students collected rainwater in large containers. They used the collected water.\",\"offset\":13600000,\"duration\":290800000},{\"text\":\"To care for the plants, after several weeks, the garden became healthy again. The students also harvested tomatoes, eggplants and other vegetables. They shared the vegetables with their families and the school\'s canteen. The students learned that working together could help solve problems in their community.\",\"offset\":305300000,\"duration\":204400000}],\"diagnostics\":{\"recognizedResults\":2,\"wordEvidence\":122,\"recognizingResults\":107,\"noMatchResults\":0,\"canceledResults\":1,\"audioBytesReceived\":1632000,\"sessionStarted\":true,\"sessionStopped\":true,\"serviceConnected\":true,\"lastRecognizedText\":\"To care for the plants, after several weeks, the garden became healthy again. The students also harvested tomatoes, eggplants and other vegetables. They shared the vegetables with their families and the school\'s canteen. The students learned that working together could help solve problems in their community.\",\"sdkVersion\":\"1.34.0\",\"jsonWordEvidence\":122,\"sdkWordEvidence\":122,\"resultJsonBytes\":83912,\"audioWriterAlive\":false,\"writerFailed\":false},\"error\":null,\"finalSeen\":true,\"doneSeen\":true},\"realtime\":{\"transcript\":\"Every Saturday morning, the students of Riverside Elementary helped care for a small community garden. The garden had vegetables, flowers, and several young fruit trees. One Saturday the student noticed that some of the plants were beginning to dry. Their teacher explained that the weather had been unusually hot and that the plants needed more water. Instead of using only the school water supply, the student collected rainwater in large containers. They used the collected water to care for the plants. After several weeks, the garden became healthy again. The students also harvested tomatoes, eggplants,